eo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-08-20T18:43:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T19:46:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7 and 4.7.1\n- Not reproducible in 4.6\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Single-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 31.74 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI can trigger this error in many different ways, so the broad issue is that taking an action in the editor results in the following error in the Output window:\n\n```\n  ERROR: scene/main/viewport.cpp:440 - Condition \"index == -1\" is true.\n```\n\nIn some cases, it seems to cause the operation to fail. In other cases, I see no impact.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFrom scratch:\n1. Open Godot.\n2. Create a new project. In my case, I chose the defaults of Create Folder, Forward+, Git, and Edit Now:<img width=\"778\" height=\"847\" alt=\"Godot new project configuration screen\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/08db249e-b8c2-428f-9cad-8447edd08881\" />\n3. Turn on Single Window Mode in Editor > Editor Settings > Interface > Editor > Single Window Mode.\n4. Create a new scene.\nExpected: The scene is created without an error.\nActual: The scene is created with an error in the Output tab.\n\nWith the scene open:\n1. Right click on the scene in the FileSystem view.\n2. Click Delete.\n3. Click Remove in the dialog.\n\nExpected: The scene is deleted without error.\nActual: The scene is not deleted and the error is output to the Output tab.\n\nWith the scene closed:\n1. Right click on the scene in the FileSystem view.\n2. Click Delete.\n3. Click Remove in the dialog.\n\nExpected: The scene is deleted without error.\nActual: The scene is deleted and the error is output to the Output tab.\n\nVideo:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79785bf1-1573-44e5-8f4c-a29b8e061c30\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[index-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31276100/index-error.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122665/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}